1614	1724	Early life
Vytenis Povilas Andriukaitis was born in Kyusyur, Yakut Autonomous Soviet Socialist Republic, USSR.
1725	1921	His father, Alfonsas Andriukaitis and mother Liuda Andriukaitienė, pregnant at the time, together with two small children were deported from Lithuania to Siberia by Soviet Communists in June 1941.
1922	2100	While there, they only had access to Russian literature; Andriukaitis learned Lithuanian from his mother, who would write down Lithuanian fairy tales, which he would later read.

2100	2188	In 1954, the family received a permission to relocate to Olyokminsk in continental USSR.
2189	2312	In 1957, they were allowed to return to Lithuania after his mother was awarded a medal of honour for raising five children.
2313	2452	The family moved to Kaunas, Lithuania – he, his mother and two brothers, Antanas and Petras, joined later by their father Alfonsas in 1959.
2453	2557	His older brothers were serving in the USSR Army – Šarūnas in Kaliningrad and Remigijus in Vladivostok.

2557	2674	Andriukaitis excelled at school and was awarded a "Gold medal" upon his graduation from Kaunas Middle School in 1969.
2675	2793	It was uncommon to be awarded a medal of achievement without being a member of the "komjaunuoliai" (Young Communists).
2794	2878	Right after graduation, he enrolled at Kaunas Medicine Institute graduating in 1975.
2879	2976	He continued his studies, pursuing a degree in history at Vilnius University, graduating in 1984.
2977	3141	He did not join the Communist party during his university years and was instead a member of the underground Social Democratic movement for independent Lithuania.



